  "notes": "The Forgotten brute's wide sweep (move forgotten-brute-sweep, 44/8/52 ticks at 60 Hz), hand-keyed (mw-ju8.25) on the greybox humanoid rig. 0-0.25 s: it drops into a wide, low stance (both knees deep). 0.25-0.68 s: a slow coil, chest and shoulders wound far round to the right with the maul trailing out and back at hip height, held 0.6-0.68 s (the telegraph). 0.68-0.87 s: one flat, low swing through the whole arc; the hit marker is on tick 44 (0.7333 s), the move's first active tick, as the maul crosses the front of the body, and the swing carries on to the left over the 8 active ticks. 0.87-1.2 s: the weight of the maul drags the torso round and it stays overextended, off balance (the long recovery to punish); then it unwinds to rest by 1.7333 s. Torso: a negative chest y winds the right shoulder back, a positive y turns it forward; arms and legs hang down, so a positive x swings them forward.",
